30
00:54:02.722 --> 00:54:07.722
Praise God. Hallelujah. Ruben and Carolien, may I invite you to the stage?

31
00:54:08.722 --> 00:54:10.722
Hallelujah.

32
00:54:12.722 --> 00:54:19.722
Okay, we are working on the Open About Relationships Month this month. Right?

33
00:54:19.722 --> 00:54:30.722
And I have explained this month that we are clearly talking about marriage. Marriage is extremely important to God.

34
00:54:30.722 --> 00:54:46.722
For God, marriage is a primary subject. One of the primary subjects for God is the marital relationship that God has with humanity and that man and woman have with each other.

35
00:54:46.722 --> 00:54:57.722
It begins in the Bible with a marriage. That is where it starts. God who initially says in His own love that He has for Himself in the Trinity.

36
00:54:57.722 --> 00:55:06.722
He says let us make man and He says it to His angelic community, the divine community. He says let us make man.

37
00:55:06.722 --> 00:55:17.722
Why? Because He has love for this world. He had love even before you could have love for Him, He had love for you and that is why you exist.

38
00:55:17.722 --> 00:55:32.722
You are chosen by God because He loves you. He loved you even before you were made. So the basis of His signs of who you are now is love. That is the foundation.

39
00:55:33.722 --> 00:55:44.722
And from that love that God has for humanity, He shows how marriage is a representation of the marriage of God to man.

40
00:55:44.722 --> 00:55:57.722
So marriage is an important subject for God. And where is the attack now particularly hard at work? The attack is on marriage.

41
00:55:57.722 --> 00:56:08.722
Satan wants only one thing, and that is for all marriages to fall apart. Satan wants only one thing: that not even one marriage is blessed in the name of Jesus.

42
00:56:08.722 --> 00:56:20.722
The name of Jesus makes him tremble and shake. And that is why it is so wonderful for the church to teach people about marriage.

43
00:56:20.722 --> 00:56:29.722
To bless them in the name of Jesus and to teach them what it truly means to love one another in marriage. Amen?

44
00:56:29.722 --> 00:56:37.722
And because we understand that this is so important, we have the new start course that we offer twice a year.

45
00:56:37.722 --> 00:56:42.722
If people want to be baptized, they need to know why they are being baptized.

46
00:56:42.722 --> 00:56:52.722
And so you first need a piece of teaching before you can make a real rational choice for Jesus, and that is called the new start course.

47
00:56:52.722 --> 00:57:00.722
In the same way, we as an open church find it very important that we also provide solid and strong teaching about marriage.

48
00:57:00.722 --> 00:57:06.722
Because people should not just step into the marriage boat and think to themselves, I like you, oh I like you too.

49
00:57:06.722 --> 00:57:13.722
Oh great, we are getting married tomorrow. And then what? Why are you getting married? With whom are you getting married? Why are you getting married?

50
00:57:13.722 --> 00:57:20.722
With whom are you getting married? Not only with whom are you getting married, but with whom are you getting married? And what does that look like?

51
00:57:20.722 --> 00:57:31.722
And it is necessary as an open church that we provide strong teaching on this, but it is also important that there is some guidance in this. Amen?

52
00:57:31.722 --> 00:57:44.722
We have therefore approached Ruben and Carolien and asked them to be pioneers in marriage ministry, in marriage guidance in the open church.

53
00:57:44.722 --> 00:57:55.722
And that means we have asked them to teach about marriage and to provide guidance in marriage situations.

54
00:57:55.722 --> 00:58:07.722
So it could be that in some time people will talk to Ruben and Carolien about perhaps the first startup year, which might not be easy.

55
00:58:07.722 --> 00:58:15.722
Last week we talked about conflict. And then it is like, yes, but there are issues, it is difficult, and we have conflict with each other, and how do we handle this?

56
00:58:15.722 --> 00:58:26.722
And precisely through a good conversation, which we also taught last week, precisely through a good conversation, it leads to you becoming stronger in your marriage.

57
00:58:26.722 --> 00:58:36.722
So many problems can be solved through a good, decent, and wise conversation with people who are married in the name of Jesus.

58
00:58:37.722 --> 00:58:44.722
For your information, these people are married. It is indeed nice in the name of Jesus.

59
00:58:44.722 --> 00:58:50.722
Married, loving Jesus, filled with the Holy Spirit.

60
00:58:50.722 --> 00:58:59.722
Already married for a number of years. How long have you been married? Next year 25. Amen. That is wonderful.

61
00:59:00.722 --> 00:59:08.722
And then you come there as a young couple, yes we have this and that, that is difficult.

62
00:59:08.722 --> 00:59:14.722
